This repository redistributes third-party data.

1. CarbonCast hourly generation by fuel
   Files: data/carboncast/CISO_direct_emissions.csv,
          data/carboncast/ERCO_direct_emissions.csv,
          data/carboncast/PJM_direct_emissions.csv
   Source: https://github.com/carbonfirst/CarbonCast
   Authors: Diptyaroop Maji, Prashant Shenoy, Ramesh K. Sitaraman,
            University of Massachusetts Amherst
   Licence: Apache License 2.0, full text in
            data/carboncast/LICENSE-Apache-2.0.md
   Files are redistributed unmodified. Derived columns are computed at runtime
   in phantomload/tracks/t4_curtailment.py and are not written back over the
   source files.

2. PJM cost of new entry parameters
   File: data/pjm_cone.csv
   Source: PJM Interconnection, "2027/2028 RPM Base Residual Auction Planning
           Period Parameters", August 26 2025, Table 3.
   Status: auction planning parameters published by PJM for public use. The
           values were transcribed from the published PDF; the transcription
           lives in tools/build_pjm_cone.py and is checked against PJM's own
           gross-minus-offset arithmetic by tests/test_tracks.py.

3. PJM average energy price
   File: data/pjm_lmp.csv
   Source: Monitoring Analytics, independent market monitor for PJM, State of
           the Market and Members Committee reports.
   Status: published market monitoring reports; the vendored file carries three
           annual figures transcribed from them.

4. FERC regional and wholesale demand response tables
   Files: data/ferc_dr_regional.csv, data/rto_dr.csv
   Source: Federal Energy Regulatory Commission, "2025 Assessment of Demand
           Response and Advanced Metering", Staff Report, December 2025.
   Status: work of the U.S. Government, not subject to domestic copyright.
           FERC compiles tables 3-1, 3-2, 5-1 and 5-2 from Form EIA-861 files
           and table 3-3 from the RTOs' and ISOs' own annual reports.

5. ACEEE utility-level demand response data, 2015
   File: data/aceee_dr_utilities_2015.csv
   Source: Steven Nadel, American Council for an Energy-Efficient Economy,
           "Demand response programs can reduce utilities' peak demand an
           average of 10%, complementing savings from energy efficiency
           programs", 9 February 2017, and its data appendix.
   Underlying data: 2015 Form EIA-861 demand response file, a U.S. Government
           work, aggregated to utility level by ACEEE.
   See PRIOR_WORK.md for what this work established before this repository did.

6. EIA-861 utility-level demand response files, 2016 to 2018
   Files: data/eia861_dr_utility_2016_2018.csv,
          data/eia861_dr_utility_class_2016_2018.csv
   Source: Form EIA-861 detailed data files, Demand_Response_<year>.xlsx,
           U.S. Energy Information Administration. Work of the U.S. Government,
           not subject to domestic copyright.
   Obtained from: IMMM-SFA/electricity_entity_boundaries, which redistributes
           the unmodified EIA files; that repository's own code is licensed BSD
           2-Clause, Copyright (c) 2019 Integrated Multi-Sector Multi-Scale
           Modeling. Only the public-domain EIA values are used here.

7. EIA-861 demand response aggregates
   File: data/eia861_dr_national.csv
   Source: U.S. Energy Information Administration, Form EIA-861, "Annual
           Electric Power Industry Report", as published in Electric Power
           Annual tables 10.3, 10.4 and 10.8.
   Status: work of the U.S. Government, not subject to domestic copyright.
   The values were transcribed from the published HTML tables; the
   transcription lives in tools/build_eia861_panel.py and is checked against
   EIA's own published totals by tests/test_data.py.

8. EIA-861 detailed files beyond demand response, 2016 to 2018
   Files: data/eia861_peaks_2016_2018.csv,
          data/eia861_meters_2016_2018.csv,
          data/eia861_dynamic_pricing_2017_2018.csv,
          data/eia861_customers_2016_2018.csv,
          data/eia861_short_form_2016_2018.csv
   Source: Form EIA-861 detailed data files Operational_Data, Advanced_Meters,
           Dynamic_Pricing, Sales_Ult_Cust and Short_Form, U.S. Energy
           Information Administration. Work of the U.S. Government, not subject
           to domestic copyright.
   Obtained from: the same IMMM-SFA/electricity_entity_boundaries repository as
           item 6, under the same terms. Selected columns are extracted
           unmodified by tools/build_eia861_context.py.

9. Form EIA-861 instructions (quoted, not redistributed)
   The definitions quoted in DATA.md and phantomload/shared/eia861.py are from
   the Form EIA-861 instructions, OMB No. 1905-0129, a U.S. Government work, as
   archived by the Public Utility Data Liberation project in
   catalyst-cooperative/pudl, docs/data_sources/eia861/.
